\f1\fs22 Sarah jumped when she heard something like a metal bucket falling down stairs. Alarm planted her hand firmly on Tony\'92s thigh. His burns made him wince.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What was that?\'92 Sarah hissed.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91A metal bucket falling down stairs.\'92 Tony took Sarah\'92s hand and was on his feet. \'91Someone is coming up the fire escape, someone who doesn\'92t know to avoid the bucket. We gotta go.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony clunked the front door open and dragged Sarah down the narrow corridor. They heard the fire door open before they reached the elevator lobby. A huge, square-headed shadow blocked their escape.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You!\'92 the shadow spat.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You!\'92 Sarah spat back, recognising the agent from Travis Teh\'92s office. Now it was her turn to drag Tony down a corridor, back to his apartment.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91What\'92s that ape want with you?\'92 Tony demanded once they were back in the apartment. He leant back against the front door, as if that would barricade it, and glared at Sarah.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Me? He wants you, you idiot!\'92 Sarah stomped around the living area hoping one of the miserable windows would open up and offer a rainbow bridge to freedom. \'91That\'92s the PAPER agent I warned you about.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony screwed his face up, confused.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah stopped pacing. \'91Before the bombing! I came to warn you, remember?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>To Tony, before the bombing was an age ago.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Open up!\'92 Three blunt, fist-sized thumps shook through the door. \'91You will return what you stole.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah pulled a tablet from her bag and went to the apartment\'92s security console in the kitchen. She made a series of frenzied erratic gestures at the tablet. \'91Come on!\'92 she told the tablet. More gestures. \'91He\'92ll be requesting your door unlocks, which it will if I can\'92t subvert the command in time.\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony, with heart bouncing around like a pinball in his ribcage, stood at the kitchen doorway, and watched Sarah work.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The font door yielded an ominous 
\f2\i click
\f1\i0 .
\f2\i \

\f1\i0 <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Tax me dead!\'92 Sarah swore.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones barrelled in and, with the speed of an apex carnivore, grabbed Tony by the throat. Momentum lifted Tony of his feet and sent him\'97with Agent Jones\'92 gorilla-size hand stilling choking him\'97into the living room, over the coffee table and into the couch. The couch thudded against the wall.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91You will give me the disc,\'92 Agent Jones said, menacing. \

\f2\i <$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Disc?
\f1\i0  
\f2\i Isn\'92t it stolen documents he\'92s looking for? 
\f1\i0 Sarah rummaged the kitchen for something she could improvise as weapon. The were no pots or pans, or rolling pins, or quality flatware, or pepper mills, or candlesticks, or wine carafes, or even gravy boats. The few items of  cutlery were disposable. 
\f2\i How do these people eat?
\f1\i0 \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones pinned Tony to the couch with a knee. \'91Tell me where it is. Where is the disc?\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony tried to gargle an answer. Agent Jones released his choke-hold.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I have no idea what you\'92re talking about,\'92 Tony pleaded. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Agent Jones clocked Tony\'92s head with the butt of his pistol. \'91This is no time for lies.\'92 He clocked Tony again.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony protested with cries of agony.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>In the tiny pantry, Sarah found a weighty carton she could use, a case of beer. She lifted it chin-high and stalked Agent Jones. She was almost there. She hefted the case above her head like a slab of bush rock.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Stop,\'92 Agent Jones said as his arm swung and the pistol cocked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah was looking straight down an uncaring barrel. On the couch, Tony twisted his hips and shifted his weight just enough to lever Agent Jones, and his arm, and his hand, and the particle pistol he was holding. Reflexively, Agent Jones pulled the trigger. The bullet struck. Frothing liquid squirted from the hole in the carton. Sarah cried out and brought it down upon Agent Jones\'92 head. He crumpled unconscious over Tony, who made hard work of pushing him aside.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah froze in the shock of the near miss. Everything was sticky and wet.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony smiled, which warmed Sarah\'92s reanimation. \'91You know,\'92 he said, \'91you\'92ll have to pay for that beer.\'92\
